# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WorkLens — repository ignore rules
#
# Security note: this file is the first line of defence against committing
# credentials or personal data. gitleaks in CI is the backstop, not the
# primary control. If you add a new tool or language to this repo, add its
# artefact and secret patterns here in the same commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Go (agent/) -----------------------------------------------------------
bin/
vendor/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
go.work
go.work.sum
# Go build and test caches, if ever redirected into the tree
.gocache/
.gomodcache/

# --- Node / TypeScript (backend/, dashboard/) ------------------------------
node_modules/
.npm/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/
dist/
build/
out/
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Next.js (dashboard/) --------------------------------------------------
.next/
.vercel/
next-env.d.ts

# --- Terraform (infra/) ----------------------------------------------------
.terraform/
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.*
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
# Variable files hold account IDs, ARNs and CIDRs — never commit them.
# The *.tfvars.example templates ARE committed.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example
# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored. Provider lock files
# are committed so every developer and CI run resolves identical providers.

# --- Environment files -----------------------------------------------------
# .env.example files ARE committed (documented placeholders, no real values).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- SQLite (agent local buffer, local test databases) ---------------------
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Secrets and key material ----------------------------------------------
*.pem
# ...except the AWS RDS public trust store. It is a published CA bundle, not a secret, and
# it has to be committed: the in-VPC Lambdas connect with DB_SSL_MODE=verify-full and have
# no route to the internet to fetch it at runtime, so it ships inside each deployment zip.
# Committing it also keeps `make backend-build` reproducible offline and in CI.
!backend/assets/rds-ca-global-bundle.pem
# ...and except Amazon's four public root CA certificates, which are the fixtures for the TLS
# pinning tests. They are published certificate authority certificates, not secrets, and the whole
# point of TestPinConstantsMatchAmazonRoots is to check the agent's compiled-in SPKI pin constants
# against the real roots — generated fixtures would only prove the test agrees with itself. Without
# these committed, `make agent-test` fails on every fresh clone and worktree.
!agent/internal/uploader/testdata/*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
credentials.json
credentials
.aws/
secrets.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
*.secret
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*.gpg
*.asc

# --- Build artefacts -------------------------------------------------------
# esbuild bundles + Lambda deployment zips produced by `make backend-build`
backend/artifacts/
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# --- Local agent runtime data (never belongs in the repo) ------------------
# Captured screenshots and queued events are personal data by definition.
queue/
screenshots/
*.png.tmp

# --- Logs and temporary files ----------------------------------------------
*.log
!scripts/*.log.example
tmp/
.tmp/
.cache/

# --- macOS -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?

# --- Windows ---------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# --- Linux -----------------------------------------------------------------
.directory
.fuse_hidden*
.nfs*

# --- Editors and IDEs ------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json.example
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.\#*
\#*\#
.project
.settings/
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project

# --- Python (only used by ad-hoc tooling scripts) --------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
